  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe downward bias when recent history shows a sharp decline (e.g., from ~65 to ~57) followed by positive sentiment spikes; forecasts often predict further drops or flatlines while true outcomes rebound sharply.",
    "Forecasts systematically underestimate volatility during high-sentiment periods, failing to capture the magnitude of subsequent price spikes seen in true outcomes.",
    "When sentiment turns positive (0.20 or 1.00) after a downtrend, the model's linear projection is too conservative and lags significantly behind the actual mean reversion or upward momentum.",
    "The model fails to account for 'mean reversion' forces when recent prices are at multi-week lows; it assumes continuation of the drop rather than a bounce back.",
    "Sentiment spikes (1.00) in the history window correlate with immediate true outcome reversals, indicating the model ignores sentiment-driven momentum shifts."
  ]
}
